    {
      "id": "e0c2190d-08fc-4ad9-99b5-20588afc08d2",
      "type": "user_prompt",
      "ts": "2026-07-21T00:41:43.010Z",
      "attrs": {
        "text": "You are fixing a test-quality defect in `tests/server/storage/test_cli_db.py` (Talium code-econ storage module). Work from `/Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ`. Canonical interpreter: **`venv/bin/python`**.\n\n## The defect\n`test_import_reports_deferred` currently calls:\n`cli_db.main([\"import\", \"--source\", \"x\", \"--config\", \"config/storage.yaml\"])`\nThe `--config` is a TOP-LEVEL option but is placed AFTER the `import` subcommand, so argparse REJECTS it (unrecognized argument) and `main` returns 1 via a parse failure — NOT via the intended path (import → `operations.import_dump` raises `NotImplementedError` → caught → returns 1 with a \"deferred\" message). So the test passes for the wrong reason and never verifies the deferred-import behavior.\n\n## Fix\nRewrite `test_import_reports_deferred` so it (a) places `--config` BEFORE the verb, and (b) asserts the deferred message is actually printed:\n```python\ndef test_import_reports_deferred(capsys):\n    code = cli_db.main([\"--config\", \"config/storage.yaml\", \"import\", \"--source\", \"x\"])\n    captured = capsys.readouterr()\n    assert code == 1\n    assert \"deferred\" in (captured.out + captured.err).lower()\n```\nThis exercises the real import→NotImplementedError→return-1 path. It is environment-independent: with `TALIUM_DB_DSN` unset, `load_config` yields `dsn=\"\"` (valid) and `import_dump` raises before any DB use. Do NOT change `cli_db.py`. Do NOT change the other test in the file.\n\n## Verify & commit\nRun `venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/server/storage/test_cli_db.py -v` — both tests must pass, and confirm (by reading the output or reasoning) that `test_import_reports_deferred` now genuinely reaches the deferred message. Also run `venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/server/storage/ -q` (no regressions). Commit: `test(storage): exercise real deferred-import path in cli_db test`.\n\n## Constraints\nNo \"Claude\" anywhere. Change only the test file.\n\n## Report\nAppend to `/Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ/.superpowers/sdd/task-10-report.md` under \"## Fix round\": the change and the test result. Reply with ONLY: Status, commit SHA + subject, one-line test result, report path.",
